Strom's patch: answer every CefClient handler an offscreen video source can
be reached through, instead of leaving it to CEF's defaults.

gstcefsrc runs CEF inside the embedding process. A default that shows UI
builds it there: a click on <input type=file> built a GTK file chooser inside
Strom on Xvfb, which tripped a GTK assertion and aborted Strom with every
pipeline in it. A default that saves writes to that process's disk: a page's
download landed in /root/Downloads without a click. Both measured in
strom-full with CEF 144.

Every CefClient handler in CEF 144 (branch 7559), and what a cefsrc does:

  Handler          Decision
  ---------------  ---------------------------------------------------------
  Audio            gstcefsrc's own: page audio into the pipeline
  Command          not used: Chrome-style only, and a windowless browser is
                   Alloy-style
  ContextMenu      THIS PATCH: menu emptied (no save as, print, view source)
  Dialog           THIS PATCH: every file dialog cancelled
  Display          THIS PATCH: console messages to the cef_console GStreamer
                   debug category only, not also to stderr, where a page
                   logging in a loop would fill the embedding process's log
  Download         THIS PATCH: every download refused
  Drag             THIS PATCH: every drop refused
  Find             not used: only reached through the embedder's API
  Focus            default: nothing is shown outside the page
  Frame            default: notifications only
  JSDialog         THIS PATCH: alert/confirm/prompt suppressed; beforeunload
                   lets the page go
  Keyboard         default: key events only reach it from remote control, and
                   the commands they could start (save, print, open) end in
                   the dialog and print paths covered here
  LifeSpan         gstcefsrc's own; popups keep this client, so every
                   decision here applies to them too
  Load             default: notifications only
  Permission       strict-network.patch answers Local Network Access; THIS
                   PATCH refuses all media access, which enable-media-stream
                   would otherwise grant without asking
  Print            not implemented on purpose: with none, CEF on Linux does
                   not print, and one would open the print path
  Render           gstcefsrc's own: frames into the pipeline
  Request          gstcefsrc's own; certificate errors and authentication
                   requests keep CEF's default, which is to cancel
